{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>For YHWH has heard that I am hated.</b> Even though when she gave birth to her first son she said, ״כִּי עַתָּה יֶאֱהָבַנִי אִישִׁי״ (Genesis 29:32) — and all the more so that he would not hate her — why then did she say, ״כִּי שְׂנוּאָה אָנֹכִי״? In any event it appears that she thought this would be so, but it did not succeed for her, for she reasoned that since a wife is only for children, and the son is loved without doubt, how can a cistern be hated while its waters are cherished? Therefore she said, ״For now my husband will love me.״ But afterward she saw that she had gone in error — for by rights her sister should have given birth to the second son, so what did YHWH give me this too for? Rather, because it is revealed before HaShem, blessed be He, that he still hates her, therefore she said, ״For YHWH has heard״ — He, blessed be He, alone examines the heart and hears all the words that a man holds with his heart; but I did not know this, for I thought that his hatred had already departed." "And it may further be so, that when she gave birth to the first son he loved her, and in the interval between the one birth and the next the bond was corrupted and he returned to his hatred, for such is the custom: at the time of birth the father rejoices over the child of his loins, and along the way he rejoices also in the wife he has taken, but as days multiply all is forgotten and his love departs. And she too spoke in prophecy, ״כִּי עַתָּה יֶאֱהָבַנִי אִישִׁי״ (Genesis 29:32) — precisely now, at the time of birth and close to birth, and not afterward. And she knew this from the great distance of his heart, that this love would not last except for the moment; therefore she said, ״For now.״ But at the second son she said, ״כִּי שְׂנוּאָה אָנֹכִי״ (Genesis 29:33), and at the third son it is stated, ״עַל כֵּן קָרָא שְׁמוֹ לֵוִי״ (Genesis 29:34) — Jacob named him, to show that he agrees with her words and that his desire is to cleave to her. But regarding the earlier sons, she gave them names that signify love, yet we did not yet see his agreement until she gave birth to the third son — then he revealed his mind, that his hatred had departed entirely."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:31:11.931172281Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}